Anyway, YANI: New container item, the scale. [a]pply to determine the
total weight of items inside. Always reads zero when levitating. Yields
different (smaller) result when used underwater. Uncursed version is mildly
inaccurate. Blessed, spot on. Cursed is wildly inaccurate, imprecise and
non-repeatable; also non-droppable. All versions are (of course) heavy.
Deli owners carry a guaranteed-cursed scale on their person.

Aside: If you want to know weight without being spoiled: Become barely
burdened with a bunch of gold in your inventory. Drop gold until you are
exactly one gold piece short of being burdened. Pick up object under
test. Drop gold until you are again one piece short of burdened. Gold
dropped in previous step is equal to weight of item (in coins).

